{
 "dur": 74.8,
 "vo": [
  {
   "id": "v01",
   "t": 0.4,
   "chunks": [
    "How does pressing a pedal",
    "make a car move?",
    "Follow the force,",
    "from foot to road."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v02",
   "t": 5.5,
   "chunks": [
    "Gas pedal first.",
    "No cable:",
    "two sensors read how far you press",
    "and tell the engine computer."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v03",
   "t": 11.86,
   "chunks": [
    "A small motor opens the throttle.",
    "Air rushes in,",
    "and fuel is added,",
    "about 14.7 to 1 by weight."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v04",
   "t": 19.68,
   "chunks": [
    "Each spark",
    "shoves a piston down.",
    "The crankshaft turns",
    "those pushes into spin."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v05",
   "t": 24.63,
   "chunks": [
    "The gearbox and differential",
    "multiply that twist:",
    "about 14 to 1",
    "in first gear."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v06",
   "t": 30.16,
   "chunks": [
    "Driveshaft and axles carry it",
    "to four hand-sized patches of rubber",
    "that push the road back.",
    "The car goes forward."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v07",
   "t": 37.7,
   "chunks": [
    "Now the brake.",
    "The pedal is a 4-to-1 lever:",
    "a 100 lb push",
    "becomes 400."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v08",
   "t": 43.71,
   "chunks": [
    "A vacuum booster",
    "uses engine suction",
    "to roughly double it.",
    "800 pounds."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v09",
   "t": 49.01,
   "chunks": [
    "That drives a one-inch",
    "master cylinder piston",
    "into the brake fluid.",
    "About 1,000 psi."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v10",
   "t": 55.04,
   "chunks": [
    "Pascal's law:",
    "that pressure acts everywhere.",
    "On caliper pistons six times bigger,",
    "it's 5,000 lb of clamp, roughly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v11",
   "t": 63.44,
   "chunks": [
    "The pads squeeze the rotors,",
    "and motion turns into heat."
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v12",
   "t": 67.4,
   "chunks": [
    "What should we take apart next?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "v13",
   "t": 69.6,
   "chunks": [
    "Congrats! You've discovered",
    "how a pedal moves a car."
   ]
  }
 ]
}